{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conditional expectation conditional expectation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md","fileName":"Conditional Expectation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conditional Expectation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 20:21\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Statistical Learning and Validation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Learning and Validation","Bayesian Classification","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"conditional expectation conditional expectation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md","fileName":"Conditional Expectation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Conditional Expectation","heading":"Conditional Expectation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A conditional expectation is the mean of an outcome among cases with specified predictor values, written as $E(Y\\mid X=x)$. Under squared-error loss, it is the prediction that minimizes expected error for those predictor values.\n\nFor a binary outcome coded zero and one, the conditional expectation equals the conditional probability of class one. This connects regression-style estimation to [[Bayesian Classification]] and other class-prediction methods.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Statistical Learning and Validation","Bayesian Classification","dataanalysisforthelifescienceswithr.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Conditional Expectation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Condi